course: dictionary
lesson: 6595
title: Nod: more than yes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To nod means to move your head down and up. Usually it means «yes», or that you agree. «Every grown-up in the room nods.» They are saying yes to Mum without using any words.
explain: A nod can also be a thing you see: «a nod of the head». You can nod to say hello to a friend across the playground, too.
explain: Nodding is body language, a message that needs no words. «Ada's so relieved she can't even speak; she just nods and runs.» The nod tells us she agreed, even though she did not speak. When a character nods, ask yourself what the nod says.
explain: Watch out for the phrases. «Nod off» means to fall asleep, often while sitting up. «Give the nod» means to give permission or approval. These phrases do not mean the movement of the head, so read the words around them.
fact: Nod means to move your head down and up.
fact: «Nodded» can replace «said yes» in a story, and it shows how a character feels.
fact: A nod usually means yes, agreement or hello, but in a few cultures head movements mean different things.
fact: «Nod off» means to fall asleep, usually without meaning to.
fact: «Give the nod» means to give permission or approval.
exercise: «Chloe read it and nodded.» What does nodded most likely show? | Chloe was angry and shouted | *Chloe agreed or accepted the apology | Chloe was lost | Chloe was fast asleep
exercise: «Mum groans, and every grown-up in the room nods.» What does the nod show? | They are falling asleep | They are shouting at Mum | They want more cake | *They agree with Mum
exercise: «The Rat is starving, but he nods and says «wonderful».» What does the nod show? | He is angry with his friend | He is falling asleep | He cannot hear what his friend said | *He agrees and is being kind, even though he is hungry
test: What does «nod off» mean? | *To fall asleep, usually without meaning to | To jump up and down | To say goodbye | To shout loudly
test: Which phrase means to give permission or approval? | *To give the nod | To nod off | To nod at a friend | A nod of the head
exam: In the sentence «She gave a nod», what kind of word is nod? | A phrase that means to fall asleep | *A noun | An adjective | A verb
